  [RISK] lib/sbi/riscv_atomic.c:15-17  (file-level preprocessor guard)
      Compile-time gate requires __riscv_atomic OR __riscv_zaamo OR __riscv_zalrsc. This is a coarse tri-state guard that does not distinguish between full Zaamo (all AMOs including AMOSwap) and Ziccamoa (AMOArithmetic only). The gate's logic is: 'some atomic support is present' = 'all AMO instructions are safe to emit', which is the root of the extension capability over-assumption. The guard itself is not wrong (it correctly ensures some atomic mechanism exists), but downstream code inside the file incorrectly infers full AMO capability from this coarse check.
  [RISK] lib/sbi/sbi_illegal_atomic.c:14-16  (file-level preprocessor guard)
